We add $\goldD{\dfrac{49}{16}}$ inside the parentheses, and subtract $\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{49}{16}}$ outside them, to keep the expression equivalent.

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\greenD{2} \left(x^2 -\dfrac{7}{2} x\right) +5
\\\\
&=\greenD{2}\left(x^2 -\dfrac{7}{2} x+\goldD{\dfrac{49}{16}}\right) +5 -\greenD{2}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{49}{16}}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x -\dfrac{7}{4}\right)^2 +5 -\dfrac{49}{8}
\\\\
&=2 \left(x -\dfrac{7}{4}\right)^2 -\dfrac{9}{8}
\end{align}$
